# Build products - what "make" writes (CLAUDE.md, Workflow Guideline 5).
#
# Scoped on purpose: nothing here may hide reference data. The real
# hardware references are *.o.golden, *.golden.base64.txt and the
# base64 text in tests/mutos1700_crt0/, tests/mutos1700_libc/ and
# mutos/mutos_bin/, and every other original file under mutos/ (headers,
# manual pages) - no pattern below matches them (Workflow Guideline 2).

# The MUTOS root, made by scripts/mutos_root.sh, removed by "make clean"
# (docs/TOOLCHAIN_PLAN.md, decision 3)
/mutos_root/

# Objects and programs under src/
/src/**/*.o
/src/mutos_ld/mutos_ld
/src/mutos_as/mutos_as
/src/mutos_as/parse_dump
/src/mutos_as/classify_test
/src/mutos_as/fltconst_test
/src/mutos_cpp/mutos_cpp
/src/mutos_cc/mutos_c0
/src/mutos_cc/mutos_c1
/src/mutos_cc/mutos_c2
/src/mutos_cc/mutos_cc
/src/mutos_cc/fltdec_test

# The objects "make test" assembles next to the .s files it checks
# (tests/mutos_as/run_goldens.sh writes <name>.o beside <name>.o.golden).
# Four of them in float_coverage/ were committed once and stay tracked;
# ignoring does not touch a tracked file.
/tests/mutos_as/*/*.o

# Python's byte-code caches (tests/realbin/ imports its own modules)
__pycache__/
